      "owasp": "API3:2023 Broken Object Property Level Authorization",
      "severity": "CRITICAL",
      "title": "Field 'role' can be set by the caller (mass assignment)",
      "endpoint": "PATCH /users/{id}",
      "detail": "The spec does not list 'role' as a writable field, but sending it in the update saved it: it was \"user\", and the object read back showed \"apifuzz-probe\" (confirmed on a second read). This field controls what the user may do, so a caller can raise their own privileges. The original value was put back afterwards.",
      "remediation": "Copy only the fields the endpoint is meant to accept from the request onto the object (an explicit allowlist or a dedicated input model), and ignore or reject everything else. Never bind the whole request body to the stored record.",
